# The disk of the persist cases (tests/cases/machine.persist.json and
# machine.persist-ahci.json): persistprobe on a KRFFS root on disk.
#
# mkdisk.sh builds it, and each case boots a private copy of it twice with
# rach2.fsdisk and rach2.rescue. The first boot writes /persist.txt and calls
# fsync and is then cut off; the second reads the file back, which shows that
# fsync took the write through the page cache to the disk.
file 0755 /persistprobe build/tests/persistprobe
